    "status": "observed",
    "title": "Hidden Windows launcher makes native startup failures look like an unexplained flash-exit",
    "summary": "Resolved Quick-Automatic-Hardsub-Encoder Windows startup regression: `Find-NativeTool` used a malformed/unsafe PowerShell `return if(...)` construct while resolving ffmpeg/ffprobe. The fix replaces it with explicit branch returns. A targeted Windows smoke assertion now executes `Find-NativeTool 'ffmpeg'` and `'ffprobe'`, and the full Windows local smoke job passed before PR #28 was squash-merged to main. The normal launcher still hides the Bridge process, so startup-failure observability remains a separate hardening concern.",
